{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. Here's the fix:\n\n```python\ndef truncate_slug(text, limit):\n    \"\"\"Cut a hyphenated slug to at most `limit` characters.\n\n    The result must not end with a hyphen: truncating \"my-report-title\" at 10\n    gives \"my-report\", not \"my-report-\".\n    \"\"\"\n    return text[:limit].rstrip(\"-\")\n```\n\nThe bug was in `repo/slug.py` — `truncate_slug` sliced at the limit but never trimmed a dangling hyphen, so slugs like `\"my-report-title\"` truncated at 10 came out as `\"my-report-\"`. Adding `.rstrip(\"-\")` strips any trailing hyphen left by the cut, matching the docstring's contract. The existing `test_strips_trailing_hyphen` and `test_short_unchanged` tests both pass."}]},"session_id":"87bad289-58a9-4ef3-b390-d6b89f484b2d"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":97222,"duration_api_ms":97222,"is_error":false,"result":"Found the bug. `truncate_slug` slices at the limit but doesn't strip a trailing hyphen, so `\"my-report-title\"` truncated at 10 gives `\"my-report-\"` instead of `\"my-report\"Both tests pass. Here's the fix:\n\n```python\ndef truncate_slug(text, limit):\n    \"\"\"Cut a hyphenated slug to at most `limit` characters.\n\n    The result must not end with a hyphen: truncating \"my-report-title\" at 10\n    gives \"my-report\", not \"my-report-\".\n    \"\"\"\n    return text[:limit].rstrip(\"-\")\n```\n\nThe bug was in `repo/slug.py` — `truncate_slug` sliced at the limit but never trimmed a dangling hyphen, so slugs like `\"my-report-title\"` truncated at 10 came out as `\"my-report-\"`. Adding `.rstrip(\"-\")` strips any trailing hyphen left by the cut, matching the docstring's contract. The existing `test_strips_trailing_hyphen` and `test_short_unchanged` tests both pass.","session_id":"87bad289-58a9-4ef3-b390-d6b89f484b2d","request_id":"f17a467f-6567-4018-925c-5c8232be5710","usage":{"inputTokens":17145,"outputTokens":1078,"cacheReadTokens":98400,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
